  "docs": {
    "api-key/create.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# api-key.create\n\nCreate an API key in an organisation. The key itself is shown once.\n\n**Who may call:** the owner of its organization.\n\n**Budget:** p95 250ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| organization | api-key.organization |\n| name | api-key.name |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| apiKey | api-key.id |\n| key | Secret (secret) |\n\n## Steps\n\n- `api-key.create.issue` (database)\n- `api-key.create.insert` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the owner of its organization; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nplugged-in api-key create --organization <organization> --name <name>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /api-key/create` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.api-key.create(payload)`.\n",
    "api-key/index.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# api-key\n\nA key an agent or a service calls with, on behalf of whoever created it. Better Auth keeps its hash.\n\nLives in the database.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | id |\n| organization | organization.id |\n| name | text |\n| createdBy | person.id |\n\n## Operations\n\n- [api-key.create](create.md): Create an API key in an organisation. The key itself is shown once.\n",
    "handle/claim.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# handle.claim\n\nClaim a free name and make it the address of your public profile.\n\n**Who may call:** anyone signed in.\n\n**Idempotent by request:** send `idempotency-key`; the same key twice is one call.\n\n**Budget:** p95 150ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| name | handle.name |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| handle | handle.id |\n\n## Move\n\n`claim`: from nothing (it creates) to claimed, emitting HandleClaimed.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `handle.claim.load` (database)\n- `handle.claim.record` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| HandleTaken | 3 | HN-001 | declared in errors.ts |\n| HandleAlreadyOwned | 4 | HN-002 | declared in errors.ts |\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't anyone signed in; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nplugged-in handle claim --name <name>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /handle/claim` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.handle.claim(payload)`.\n",
    "handle/index.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# handle\n\nA public name that belongs to one person until they release it.\n\nLives in the database.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | id |\n| name | HandleName |\n| owner | person.id |\n\n## Machine\n\nStates: claimed, released. A move from the wrong state is refused HandleNotClaimed (exit 5).\n\n| move | from | to | emits |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| claim | (creates) | claimed | HandleClaimed |\n| release | claimed | released | HandleReleased |\n\n## Roles\n\n- handleOwner\n\n## Operations\n\n- [handle.claim](claim.md): Claim a free name and make it the address of your public profile.\n- [handle.release](release.md): Free your name and take its public profile offline.\n- [handle.resolve](resolve.md): Find the handle for a claimed name.\n",
    "handle/release.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# handle.release\n\nFree your name and take its public profile offline.\n\n**Who may call:** the handleOwner of the handle.\n\n**Budget:** p95 150ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| handle | handle.id |\n\n## Answer\n\n(none)\n\n## Move\n\n`release`: from claimed to released, emitting HandleReleased.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `handle.release.record` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| HandleNotClaimed | 5 | HN-900 | the handle is in a state release can't start from; carries `state` |\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the handleOwner of the handle; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nplugged-in handle release --handle <handle>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /handle/release` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.handle.release(payload)`.\n",
    "handle/resolve.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# handle.resolve\n\nFind the handle for a claimed name.\n\n**Who may call:** anyone.\n\n**Budget:** p95 150ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| name | handle.name |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| handle | handle.id |\n\n## Steps\n\n- `handle.resolve.load` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| HandleNotFound | 6 | HN-003 | declared in errors.ts |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nplugged-in handle resolve --name <name>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /handle/resolve` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.handle.resolve(payload)`.\n",
    "invitation/accept.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# invitation.accept\n\nAccept an invitation and become a member of its organisation.\n\n**Who may call:** the invitee of the invitation.\n\n**Budget:** p95 200ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| invitation | invitation.id |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| organization | invitation.organization |\n| membership | membership.id |\n\n## Move\n\n`accept`: from pending to accepted, emitting InvitationAccepted.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `invitation.accept.join` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| InvitationNotPending | 40 | IN-900 | the invitation is in a state accept can't start from; carries `state` |\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the invitee of the invitation; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nplugged-in invitation accept --invitation <invitation>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /invitation/accept` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.invitation.accept(payload)`.\n",
    "invitation/index.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# invitation\n\nAn offer to join an organisation, sent to an email address.\n\nLives in the database.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | id |\n| organization | organization.id |\n| email | person.email |\n| invitedBy | person.id |\n\n## Machine\n\nStates: pending, accepted, revoked. A move from the wrong state is refused InvitationNotPending (exit 40).\n\n| move | from | to | emits |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| send | (creates) | pending | InvitationSent |\n| accept | pending | accepted | InvitationAccepted |\n| revoke | pending | revoked | InvitationRevoked |\n\n## Roles\n\n- invitee\n\n## Operations\n\n- [invitation.accept](accept.md): Accept an invitation and become a member of its organisation.\n- [invitation.revoke](revoke.md): Withdraw an invitation that hasn't been accepted.\n- [invitation.send](send.md): Invite someone to an organisation by email.\n",
    "invitation/revoke.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# invitation.revoke\n\nWithdraw an invitation that hasn't been accepted.\n\n**Who may call:** the owner of its invitation.organization.\n\n**Budget:** p95 150ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| invitation | invitation.id |\n\n## Answer\n\n(none)\n\n## Move\n\n`revoke`: from pending to revoked, emitting InvitationRevoked.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `invitation.revoke.update` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| InvitationNotPending | 40 | IN-900 | the invitation is in a state revoke can't start from; carries `state` |\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the owner of its invitation.organization; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nplugged-in invitation revoke --invitation <invitation>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /invitation/revoke` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.invitation.revoke(payload)`.\n",
    "invitation/send.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# invitation.send\n\nInvite someone to an organisation by email.\n\n**Who may call:** the owner of its organization.\n\n**Budget:** p95 200ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| organization | invitation.organization |\n| email | invitation.email |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| invitation | invitation.id |\n\n## Move\n\n`send`: from nothing (it creates) to pending, emitting InvitationSent.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `invitation.send.insert` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the owner of its organization; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nplugged-in invitation send --organization <organization> --email <email>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /invitation/send` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.invitation.send(payload)`.\n",
    "link/add.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# link.add\n\nAppend a link to your public profile.\n\n**Who may call:** anyone signed in.\n\n**Idempotent by request:** send `idempotency-key`; the same key twice is one call.\n\n**Budget:** p95 150ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| title | link.title |\n| url | link.url |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| link | link.id |\n\n## Move\n\n`add`: from nothing (it creates) to listed, emitting LinkAdded.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `link.add.load` (database)\n- `link.add.record` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| LinkNeedsHandle | 4 | LI-001 | declared in errors.ts |\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't anyone signed in; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nplugged-in link add --title <title> --url <url>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /link/add` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.link.add(payload)`.\n",
    "link/index.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# link\n\nA title and web address on a person's public profile.\n\nLives in the database.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | id |\n| owner | person.id |\n| title | LinkTitle |\n| url | LinkUrl |\n\n## Machine\n\nStates: listed, removed. A move from the wrong state is refused LinkNotListed (exit 5).\n\n| move | from | to | emits |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| add | (creates) | listed | LinkAdded |\n| remove | listed | removed | LinkRemoved |\n\n## Roles\n\n- linkOwner\n\n## Operations\n\n- [link.add](add.md): Append a link to your public profile.\n- [link.order](order.md): Move a link to a zero-based position. A position past the end puts it last.\n- [link.remove](remove.md): Remove one of your links from your public profile.\n",
    "link/order.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# link.order\n\nMove a link to a zero-based position. A position past the end puts it last.\n\n**Who may call:** the linkOwner of the link.\n\n**Budget:** p95 150ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| link | link.id |\n| position | LinkPosition |\n\n## Answer\n\n(none)\n\n## Steps\n\n- `link.order.load` (database)\n- `link.order.record` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| LinkAlreadyRemoved | 6 | LI-002 | declared in errors.ts |\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the linkOwner of the link; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nplugged-in link order --link <link> --position <position>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /link/order` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.link.order(payload)`.\n",
    "link/remove.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# link.remove\n\nRemove one of your links from your public profile.\n\n**Who may call:** the linkOwner of the link.\n\n**Budget:** p95 150ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| link | link.id |\n\n## Answer\n\n(none)\n\n## Move\n\n`remove`: from listed to removed, emitting LinkRemoved.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `link.remove.record` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| LinkNotListed | 5 | LI-900 | the link is in a state remove can't start from; carries `state` |\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the linkOwner of the link; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nplugged-in link remove --link <link>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /link/remove` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.link.remove(payload)`.\n",
    "membership/get.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# membership.get\n\nRead one membership by its id: organization, person, role.\n\n**Who may call:** the holder of the membership, or the owner of its membership.organization.\n\n**A read:** answered from the records, with no handler.\n\n**Budget:** p95 50ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | membership.id |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| organization | membership.organization |\n| person | membership.person |\n| role | membership.role |\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the holder of the membership, or the owner of its membership.organization; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nplugged-in membership get --id <id>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /membership/get` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.membership.get(payload)`.\n",
    "membership/index.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# membership\n\nA person's place in an organisation.\n\nLives in the database.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | id |\n| organization | organization.id |\n| person | person.id |\n| role | Role |\n\n## Roles\n\n- holder\n\n## Operations\n\n- [membership.get](get.md): Read one membership by its id: organization, person, role.\n",
    "organization/create.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# organization.create\n\nFound an organisation. Whoever founds it owns it, and is its first member.\n\n**Who may call:** anyone signed in.\n\n**Idempotent by request:** send `idempotency-key`; the same key twice is one call.\n\n**Budget:** p95 250ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| name | organization.name |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| organization | organization.id |\n\n## Move\n\n`create`: from nothing (it creates) to active, emitting OrganizationCreated.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `organization.create.insert` (database)\n- `organization.create.owner` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't anyone signed in; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nplugged-in organization create --name <name>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /organization/create` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.organization.create(payload)`.\n",
    "organization/get.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# organization.get\n\nRead one organization by its id: name, owner, state.\n\n**Who may call:** the owner of the organization.\n\n**A read:** answered from the records, with no handler.\n\n**Budget:** p95 50ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | organization.id |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| name | organization.name |\n| owner | organization.owner |\n| state | text |\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the owner of the organization; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nplugged-in organization get --id <id>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /organization/get` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.organization.get(payload)`.\n",
    "organization/index.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# organization\n\nA company or team that people belong to.\n\nLives in the database.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | id |\n| name | text |\n| owner | person.id |\n\n## Machine\n\nStates: active. A move from the wrong state is refused OrganizationNotActive (exit 20).\n\n| move | from | to | emits |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| create | (creates) | active | OrganizationCreated |\n\n## Roles\n\n- owner\n\n## Operations\n\n- [organization.create](create.md): Found an organisation. Whoever founds it owns it, and is its first member.\n- [organization.get](get.md): Read one organization by its id: name, owner, state.\n",
    "person/index.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# person\n\nSomeone who signs in. Better Auth keeps people; the project refers to them by id.\n\nLives in the database.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | id |\n| email | text |\n| name | text |\n\n## Operations\n\n- [person.sign-up](sign-up.md): Sign up with an email address and a password.\n",
