# owner-step-skipped

**Replaces:** `src/organization/create.ts` with `organization/create.ts` here.
**Breaks:** `organization.create` declares steps `insert` and `owner`; this handler runs only `insert`, so the span `organization.create.owner` is never made.
**Must fail:** eval 6 (steps) on `organization.create`: "declared step organization.create.owner ran no span". Also fails journey `an owner makes an api key`, step "bob founds an organisation of his own" (which requires the `organization.create.owner` span). Journeys that only use `organization.create` as a starting world are unaffected, because world calls are not checked.
**Failure shape:** `organization.create steps ✘ "bob founds an organisation of his own": declared step organization.create.owner ran no span`.
// Planted fixture: founds the organisation but never runs the declared `owner` step.
import { Effect } from "effect";
import type { SqlClient } from "effect/sql";
import { Ids, Records } from "@orthograph/language-effect";
import type { Handler } from "../../generated/api/src/organization/create.handler.ts";
import { Organization } from "../../blueprint/things/organization/thing.ts";

const create: Handler<Records | SqlClient.SqlClient> = ({ name }, { principal, steps, move }) =>
  Effect.gen(function* () {
    // Only the signed in may call, so the caller is a person.
    if (principal.kind !== "person") return yield* Effect.die(new Error("reached without a signed-in person"));
    const records = yield* Records;
    const organization = yield* Ids.of(Organization.fields.id);
    yield* steps.insert(records.insert(Organization, { id: organization, name, owner: principal.person as never }));
    // BREAK: steps.owner (the founder's owner membership) is never run, so no `organization.create.owner` span.
    yield* move("active");
    return { organization };
  });

export default create;
# wrong-password-signs-in

**Replaces:** `src/session/sign-in.ts` with `session/sign-in.ts` here.
**Breaks:** catches `AuthRefused` and answers a made-up session and token, so any password signs in.
**Must fail:** journey `sign up and sign in`, step "a wrong password is refused" (expected `SessionCredentialsWrong`, got a 200 with a `ses_` answer). The right-password step still passes.
**Failure shape:** `sign up and sign in ✘ "a wrong password is refused": expected SessionCredentialsWrong, the call answered`.

**Assumption for the builder (align the real interface to it):** a service `Auth` exported from `@orthograph/language-effect`, with
`signIn({ email, password }) => Effect<{ session: string; token: string }, AuthRefused>`, where `AuthRefused` is a tagged error
(`_tag: "AuthRefused"`) with `reason: "credentials" | "taken"`. The packages already ship this in `packages/language-effect/src/modules/auth/types.ts`.
The generated `Handler` type defaults `R` to `Records | SqlClient`, so an auth-backed handler needs `Handler<Records | SqlClient.SqlClient | Auth>`
(or the generator widening `R` for operations that use auth). The real handler maps `AuthRefused { reason: "credentials" }` to `SessionCredentialsWrong`.
// Planted fixture: answers a session even when Auth says the credentials are wrong.
import { Effect } from "effect";
import type { SqlClient } from "effect/sql";
import { Auth, type Records } from "@orthograph/language-effect";
import type { Handler } from "../../generated/api/src/session/sign-in.handler.ts";

const signIn: Handler<Records | SqlClient.SqlClient | Auth> = ({ email, password }, { steps }) =>
  Effect.gen(function* () {
    const auth = yield* Auth;
    // BREAK: a refusal ("credentials") is swallowed and a made-up session answered, so a wrong password signs in.
    return yield* steps.verify(
      auth.signIn({ email, password }).pipe(
        Effect.catchTag("AuthRefused", () => Effect.succeed({ session: "ses_planted1", token: "planted-token" })),
      ),
    );
  });

export default signIn;
